## Install

1. Make sure the **Input System** package (`com.unity.inputsystem`) is installed in
   Package Manager. Set Edit → Project Settings → Player → Active Input Handling to
   "Input System Package" (or "Both") and let Unity restart.
2. Drop the `Input/{{ s.name }}.inputactions` file into your `Assets/`.
3. Drop the `Scripts/` files into `Assets/Scripts/`.
{% if s.use_input_reader_so %}
4. Right-click in the Project window → **Create → Input → {{ s.name }} Reader** to
   create a `{{ s.name }}InputReader` ScriptableObject asset. Assign the
   `{{ s.name }}.inputactions` asset to its `asset` field.
5. Subscribe to its typed events from your game code:

```csharp
public class Player : MonoBehaviour
{
    [SerializeField] private {{ s.name }}InputReader input;

    private void OnEnable()
    {
{% for m in s.maps %}
{% for a in m.actions %}
{% if a.control_type == "Vector2" %}
        input.On{{ a.name }} += v => Debug.Log($"{{ a.name }}: {v}");
{% elif a.control_type == "Axis" %}
        input.On{{ a.name }} += v => Debug.Log($"{{ a.name }}: {v}");
{% else %}
        input.On{{ a.name }} += () => Debug.Log("{{ a.name }} pressed");
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
    }
}
```
{% endif %}
{% if s.use_typed_wrapper %}
6. Alternatively, use the static `{{ s.name }}Bindings` wrapper for polled access:

```csharp
// Once at startup:
{{ s.name }}Bindings.Asset = inputActionAssetReference;

// Then anywhere:
if ({{ s.name }}Bindings.Player.Jump.WasPressedThisFrame()) { /* ... */ }
```
